theorem a-calculation-asks-no-membership
  note        A calculation only joins: its orders fold over the extended
              reals each link puts its terms in, so nothing says 2·k! ∈ ℝ
              and nothing need.
  let k ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  let y ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  assume y ≤ 2·k!                                                     (H3)
  assume 2·k! < 2·k!·2                                                (H4)
  then y < 2·k!·2

1.  y < 2·k!·2
    calculation
      y ≤ 2·k!            H3
        < 2·k!·2          H4
